WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.280
How do you switch one cell type on or off in a living mouse?

2
00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:08.220
Many kinds of neurons sit tangled together in one tissue.

3
00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:12.580
Watching them fire shows when they act, not what they cause.

4
00:00:15.683 --> 00:00:19.583
First, mouse genetics puts an actuator into one cell type.

5
00:00:20.843 --> 00:00:25.523
An actuator is an engineered protein that starts or stops cell activity.

6
00:00:26.883 --> 00:00:29.343
A stop flanked by loxP sites blocks the gene.

7
00:00:30.703 --> 00:00:35.123
Only cells making Cre recombinase delete that stop, switching it on permanently.

8
00:00:36.383 --> 00:00:42.683
In chemogenetics, targeted cells build a DREADD: a designer receptor activated only

9
00:00:42.683 --> 00:00:44.023
by a synthetic ligand.

10
00:00:45.163 --> 00:00:48.823
That ligand drifts through tissue but ignores every other cell.

11
00:00:50.503 --> 00:00:54.323
Driving the targeted cells tests whether they are sufficient for a response.

12
00:00:55.723 --> 00:00:57.843
Quieting them tests whether they are necessary.

13
00:00:58.983 --> 00:01:03.463
Genetic silencing can also quiet cells without a designer receptor.

14
00:01:04.903 --> 00:01:09.923
You can silence transmitter release, or permanently remove cells, called ablation,

15
00:01:10.283 --> 00:01:11.603
with diphtheria toxin.

16
00:01:13.043 --> 00:01:16.663
Reversible inhibition tests whether cells are needed right now.

17
00:01:17.803 --> 00:01:21.583
A genetic switch turns one cell type on or off to test its role.

18
00:01:22.633 --> 00:01:23.953
Pause and predict.

19
00:01:25.713 --> 00:01:30.513
Suppose excitatory spinal neurons help drive defensive responses to mechanical

20
00:01:30.513 --> 00:01:36.673
touch. You put an inhibitory designer receptor in those neurons and give the ligand.

21
00:01:37.853 --> 00:01:40.973
Should the force needed to make the mouse pull away rise or fall?

22
00:01:46.567 --> 00:01:53.027
It rises. Quieting those excitatory neurons makes the mouse less sensitive to

23
00:01:53.027 --> 00:01:58.907
mechanical touch. Its mechanical withdrawal threshold rises, meaning it takes

24
00:01:58.907 --> 00:02:01.227
stronger force before the mouse pulls away.

25
00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:04.040
Genetic tools can mislead.

26
00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:09.860
Cre marking is permanent, capturing any cell that ever expressed the driver.

27
00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:15.640
Drivers can be leaky in wrong cells, or mosaic, missing target cells.

28
00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:22.200
Reporter light misses leftover target protein, so measure driver range and target

29
00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.820
loss directly in tissue.

30
00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:27.990
With those checks, these tools unlocked key findings.

31
00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:34.910
In 2013, Vrontou and colleagues put a DREADD in MrgprB4 neurons.

32
00:02:36.350 --> 00:02:41.030
Activating those hairy-skin sensory neurons gave male mice conditioned place

33
00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:45.630
preference. They spent more time in the chamber paired with activation.

34
00:02:47.117 --> 00:02:53.337
In 2014, Duan and colleagues ablated spinal somatostatin-lineage neurons with

35
00:02:53.337 --> 00:02:58.697
diphtheria toxin. Four weeks later, tissue counts confirmed depletion.

36
00:03:00.597 --> 00:03:05.517
Controls averaged 105 ± 4 neurons per lumbar hemisection.

37
00:03:06.837 --> 00:03:09.717
Ablated mice fell to 17 ± 2.

38
00:03:10.697 --> 00:03:14.797
Those are averages across three mice per group, plus their uncertainty.

39
00:03:14.797 --> 00:03:21.117
Ablation impaired acute and injury-associated mechanical defensive behaviour.

40
00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:25.320
Reversible tools strengthen a different inference.

41
00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:32.260
In 2016, Christensen and colleagues used chemogenetic inhibition on spinal

42
00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:34.760
somatostatin neurons in naive mice.

43
00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:41.720
Mechanical withdrawal thresholds rose, and thermal withdrawal latency lengthened, so

44
00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:43.240
mice took longer to pull away.

45
00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:48.700
Switching one genetic cell type on or off tests what it actually does.
